OL,3,GNEWSABaby termination was 'our most
OL,4,Aloving choice'
OL,5,
OL,6,FA woman whose baby was too ill to be
OL,7,Fborn is calling for better awareness of
OL,8,Fchoosing a termination for medical
OL,9,Freasons.
OL,11,FRosanna Brown, who lives near
OL,12,FWaterlooville, Hampshire, was advised
OL,13,Fto end her pregnancy with son William
OL,14,Fin 2023 because he had a rare and
OL,15,Flife-threatening medical condition
OL,16,Fcalled Chaos syndrome.
OL,18,FContinuing the pregnancy would have
OL,19,Frisked both their lives, but Rosanna
OL,20,Fsaid the experience was made even more
OL,21,Fdifficult due to a lack of training
OL,22,Faround medically-advised abortions.
